From 6bf6d9bc44cff364b039fcb3b1c4a3fa5a57bb15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:43:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] sensor: Add the tilt to wake gesture sensor

Qualcomm's sns_tilt_to_wake algorithm runs on the Sensor Core and reports
one event each time the device is raised towards the user, with wake-up
delivery. Expose it as SSCSensorTiltToWake with a "detected" signal and
add it to ssccli. Gesture sensors report a single-output stream type:
enable any non-continuous sensor like an on-change one instead of
asserting.
